{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And Korah took.</b> An expression of taking men. And whom did he take? Datan and Aviram, sons of Eliav, and On son of Pelet, sons of Reuven. The vav of ודתן is superfluous, and there are many like it." "<b>Sons of Reuven.</b> Eliav and Pelet. Pelet is Peleu, and Eliav is his son, as it is written: ״ובני פלוא אליאב״. And since it said above, ״במדבר הזה יתמו ושם ימותו״, it begins to tell how some of them died on account of Korah, and some of them in the plague, and some of them in Shittim, until none of them remained."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:18:10.008863697Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}